# Environment for the field app (apps/fieldApp). Copy this file to `.env` and edit it; `.env` is ignored by git.
# Expo only exposes variables that start with EXPO_PUBLIC_ to the app, and they are baked in when the app is bundled,
# so never put a secret here. Restart `expo start` (add --clear) after changing a value.

# The API's base URL, including the `/api` prefix, with no trailing slash.
#
# Leave it unset while developing: the app then works it out from the machine running the Expo dev server
# (http://<that machine's LAN IP>:3000/api), so a phone in Expo Go reaches the API on your PC. Android emulator: 10.0.2.2.
# Set it for a build that talks to a deployed server, or when the API is not on the same machine as the dev server.
#
# Examples:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.20:3000/api
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api
#EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
